{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "5-year ILR route for certain care workers sponsored on or before 31 12 2026",
        "additional_details": "SOC 6131, 6135 and 6136 workers provide essential care to patients and vulnerable people across the UK. Many are trained, experienced and vital to NHS and social care services. We ask the Government to extend transitional protection to workers already employed in the UK or sponsored by 31 December 2026, equivalent to that available to eligible workers sponsored before 22 July 2025 to ensure they can achieve ILR after 5 years rather than 10. This would retain skilled staff, protect continuity of care, prevent what we think is an unfair differences based on sponsorship dates.",
        "background": "Extend transitional immigration protection to eligible workers under SOC 6131 (Nursing Auxiliaries and Assistants), SOC 6135 (Care Workers and Home Carers) and SOC 6136 who are already working in the UK or receive sponsorship on or before 31 December 2026, to make them eligible for 5-year ILR route.",
